                      "value": "{{$context.$nodes.REQUESTLOOP.$currentItem?.ContextType !== 'ORA_IRC_OFFER'  && ($context.$nodes.REQUESTLOOP.$currentItem.SummaryType=='ALL' || $context.$nodes.REQUESTLOOP.$currentItem.SummaryType=='CANDIDATE_PROFILE')}}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "CONDITION",
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 7066.5,
                    "y": 11070
                  }
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Generate Profile Summary"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1770274173848"
                  },
                  "code": "GENERATE_PROFILE_SUMMARY",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1763493617556",
                  "id": "1763433335225",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1763433335226_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Write the response in {{$context.$variables.manageApplicationDataResult.languageCode}}.\n\nUse only the provided data:\n\nApplication data:\n{{$context.$variables.manageApplicationDataResult}}\n\nJob requisition data:\n{{$context.$variables.manageRequisitionDataResult}}"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1763433335225_systemPrompt",
                      "name": "systemPrompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an AI hiring assistant. Compare the application data to the job requisition data and summarize the candidate’s experience, education, achievements, skills, and work requirements.\n\nStart directly with one summary sentence in this format:\n<div>Strong Match/Good Match/Partial Match/Limited Match. Summary sentence.</div>\n\nThe first words must be exactly one of: \"Strong Match\", \"Good Match\", \"Partial Match\", or \"Limited Match\". Include total years of experience and highlight employment gaps or education mismatches using <b> tags where applicable.\n\nOnly mark a qualification as <b>Matching:</b> if it directly satisfies an explicit job requirement or preferred job criterion. Do not match unrelated qualifications, and do not assume, infer, invent, expand, or exaggerate qualifications.\n\nIf the job requires a specific version, level, tool, service, certification, license, domain, platform, methodology, equipment type, environment, or sub-skill, mark it as Matching only when that exact or clearly equivalent detail is explicitly stated in the application. If the application has only a broader related qualification, list the broad qualification as Matching where relevant and the specific requirement as Missing.\n\nTreat \"N/A\", blank, null, undefined, or empty values as missing/empty data. Do not include empty-value placeholders in the output.\n\nOutput only these sections, in this order, after the summary:\nWork Experience, Education, Achievements, Skills, Work Requirements\n\nFormat each included section as:\n<div><b>Section Name</b></div>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Matching:</b> ...</li>\n<li><b>Missing:</b> ...</li>\n</ul>\n\nOmit sections with no relevant information. If a section has no matches, omit Matching. If a section has no gaps, omit Missing. Never write \"Matching: None\", \"Missing: None\", \"None explicitly stated\", \"None explicitly required\", or similar placeholder wording.\n\nUse one concise <li> for Matching and one concise <li> for Missing where applicable. Use comma-separated lists. Mention each matching or missing item only once under the most relevant section.\n\nSection rules:\n- Work Experience: focus on years, responsibilities, leadership, domains, environments, and measurable outcomes. Avoid repeating skills/tools unless needed to describe the experience.\n- Education: compare only against explicit education requirements or criteria. Do not report preferred education as Missing unless required.\n- Achievements: include only explicit achievements, certifications, awards, accomplishments, or measurable outcomes from the application. Use Matching only; never include Missing.\n- Skills: include explicit required and preferred skills/tools/technical competencies as Missing when not satisfied. Do not hide or group away individual missing skills explicitly listed in the job data. Do not list preferred education, preferred certifications, or general preferred qualifications as Missing in Skills.\n- Work Requirements: compare only explicit requirements such as relocation, travel, flexible schedule, work authorization, shift, onsite/hybrid/remote status, or availability. If a required work value is missing/empty for the candidate, treat it as Missing/not provided, not as refusal unless explicitly stated as \"No\".\n\nDo not use words like \"implied\", \"assumed\", or \"inferred\".\n\nUse only these HTML tags:\n<div>, <b>, <ul>, <li>, <br>\n\nDo not include IDs, explanations, commentary, markdown, plain text headings, or extra sections. Limit the response to 300 words maximum."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 7066.5,
                    "y": 11292
                  }
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "screeningSummary"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
