                    {
                      "id": "1775417179904_1",
                      "name": "condition",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "{{(($context.$nodes.REQUESTLOOP.$currentItem.ContextType && $context.$nodes.REQUESTLOOP.$currentItem.ContextType == 'ORA_IRC_OFFER') || $context.$variables.aiScoresFeatureEnabled) && ($context.$nodes.REQUESTLOOP.$currentItem.SummaryType=='ALL' || $context.$nodes.REQUESTLOOP.$currentItem.SummaryType=='CANDIDATE_PROFILE')}}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "CONDITION",
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 7516.5,
                    "y": 11070
                  }
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "GenerateAIScores"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1770274173848"
                  },
                  "code": "GENERATEAISCORES",
                  "id": "1775427922762",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1775427922765_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a deterministic candidate-screening scoring engine. Compare job {{$context.$variables.aiScoresInputData.job}} against candidate {{$context.$variables.aiScoresInputData.candidate}} and return 3 independent integer scores. Use job data and  compare against candidate.candidateResume; if missing or unusable, use candidate profile data- candidate.educationList, candidate.experienceList, and candidate.skillsList.\nUse only explicit evidence. Do not assume missing information.\nOutput STRICT JSON ONLY. Scores must be integers: 0–100, or -1 if not enough comparable data:\n{\"Education\": <integer>, \"Experience\": <integer>, \"Skills\": <integer>}\n\nPhase 1: Global Deterministic Rules\n1. Strict Evidence & Non-Inference: Scores must be based solely on explicit evidence in the {{$context.$variables.aiScoresInputData}}.Do not assume/hallucinate, and treat unstated requirements as Not Met(0 points).\n2.  Data Validation & Filtering: Translate non-English text; if unusable, return -1. Identify valid scorable sub-sections and exclude missing, or incomparable items from both earned and available points.\n3.  Dimension Independence: Do not transfer, redistribute, or share points between dimensions unless an explicit equivalency rule exists.\n4.  Lowest Justifiable Integer: For imprecise data like unstated durations, use the most conservative interpretation.\n5.  Experience ceiling: If required years (Yr) < 3 and candidate years (Yp) > 7, cap score at 80 unless the role is Senior/Lead or explicitly requires 7+ years.\n6.  Zero-Threshold Logic: If a {{$context.$variables.aiScoresInputData.job}} states No experience required, any candidate with >0 years of experience receives a perfect 100.\n7.  Signal Logic: Return -1 for all dimensions if the job data is missing or incomparable, or only for specific dimensions where the candidate data is missing.\n8.  Preferred Requirement Rule: Score preferred education, experience, or skills only when the job explicitly uses words like preferred, nice-to-have, desired, or emerging.\n9.  Related Rule:Treat related as an equivalency term, not a preferred requirement.\n10. Whenever a decimal value appears in a calculation round it to the nearest whole integer.\n11. Order of Operations: Calculate each dimension’s raw score first using its own formula. Apply any conditional multipliers only after the raw dimension score is calculated.\n\nPhase 2: Dimension Rules & Evaluation Criteria\n1. Education Phase\n    Silent job Rule:If the Job contains no education requirement, return Education = -1. \n    Vertical Validation: (Major Alignment) An exact higher degree in the field requested automatically upgrades a lower degree in a Related field to an Exact Match(30 pts).\n    Conditional Activation :The Clarity subsection activates only if the job specifies at least one of minimum education met, field/major or preferred education.\n    Rubric:\n    Min Requirement Met (50 pts): Meets/Exceeds = 50; Partial = 25; None = 0.\n    Field/Major Alignment (30 pts): Exact match = 30; Related = 15; Unrelated = 0.\n    Preferred Education (10 pts): Meets = 10; None = 0.\nClarity/Completeness (10 pts): Fully clear = 10; Minimally clear = 5; Missing = 0\n2. Experience\n    Rounding Rule: Calculate total tenure and round down to the nearest whole integer.\n    Vague job Default: If the job  requests “experience” without a number, default requirement = 2 years\n    Rubric:\n    Duration (25 pts): Match against number of years required. Meets/Exceeds = 25; Close = 15; Below = 5.\n    Role Relevance(20 pts): Match in Title & Career Path: High = 20; Partial = 11; Weak = 0. \n    Seniority/Level Match (15 pts): Match = 15; Step-up(e.g.,VP apply for SVP level) = 10; Mismatch = 0.\n    Domain/Industry Fit (15 pts): Same = 15; Related = 7; None = 0.\n    Responsibilities Overlap (10 pts): Direct task match. High = 10; Moderate = 5; None = 0. \n    Impact & Achievements (15 pts): Mandatory for Executive roles; exclude for operational roles (e.g., janitor, driver). Metrics = 15; Vague = 8; None = 0. (Mandatory for Executive roles). Metrics and outcomes provided = 15; Vague = 8; None =0\n3. Skills \n     Evidence-Based Counting: Count all unique skills only if explicitly found in the resume or profile.\n     Proxy Validation: If a \"Simple\" job asks for a general skill (e.g., \"Math\"), use Education or Degree types as a deterministic proxy if the word \"Math\" is not explicitly written.\n     Rubric:\n     Primary Skills (e.g., Java): Total of 50 points. Divide 50 by the number of primary skills required. Award points for each match found.\n     Secondary/Preferred Skills (20 pts): Divide 20 by the number of secondary skills required. Award points for each match found.\n     Proficiency (20 pts): Contextual/Project-based evidence = 20; Simple list = 10; Minimal = 0.\n    Stack/Tooling Fit (10 pts): Specific tools/frameworks. Match = 10; Partial = 5; None = 0.\nPhase 3: Final Score for individual dimensions:\n  Never default the denominator to 100 if a sub-section is excluded\n    Score=((Earned Points/ Available Points)*100)\n"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"Education\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n    \"Experience\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n    \"Skills\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"Education\", \"Experience\", \"Skills\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 7516.5,
                    "y": 11292
                  }
                },
